---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getApp, COMPANY } from '../../data/apps';

const app = getApp('cairn')!;
const updatedDate = 'August 22, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${app.name} Support — ${COMPANY.name}`}
  description={`Help with ${app.name} access, purchases, iCloud sync, offline study, reminders, widgets, and Live Activities.`}
  path={`/${app.slug}/support`}
  noindex={true}
  socialImage="/apps/cairn.png"
  socialImageAlt="Cairn app icon"
>
  <article class="prose container">
    <a class="back-link" href="/cairn">← {app.name}</a>
    <h1>{app.name} Support</h1>
    <p class="updated">Updated: {updatedDate}</p>

    <p>
      {app.name} is a native Microsoft certification exam-prep app for iPhone
      and iPad. It has no account or login. Version 3.0 build 2 was rejected,
      the combined app-and-IAP submission remains unresolved, and there is no
      public App Store listing.
    </p>

    <p class="callout">
      <strong>Need direct help?</strong> Email
      <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a> with your device
      model, iOS or iPadOS version, {app.name} version, and a description of what
      happened. Do not send payment-card details.
    </p>

    <h2>Current build access and Full Exam Library</h2>
    <p>
      In the current internal build, the eight Courses and complete AI-901
      workspace do not require a purchase. The proposed one-time,
      non-consumable <strong>Full Exam Library</strong> is priced at $14.99 in
      the United States submission and is still in review. It is not publicly
      purchasable, and there is no {app.name} subscription or account.
    </p>
    <p>
      Apple’s App Store and StoreKit handle purchases, payment details, refunds,
      Family Sharing, and restores. {COMPANY.name} does not receive your
      payment-card details.
    </p>

    <h2>Restore a purchase in an authorized test build</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Connect to the internet and confirm the device is using the same Apple
        Account that made or received the purchase.
      </li>
      <li>
        Open {app.name}’s purchase screen and choose
        <strong>Restore Purchases</strong>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Allow StoreKit time to refresh the entitlement, then reopen the exam
        library if it does not update immediately.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If the purchase still does not appear, check the Apple Account’s purchase
      history and Family Sharing settings. Apple Support can help with billing,
      refunds, or an App Store transaction that is missing from the account.
      These steps do not imply public availability.
    </p>

    <h2>Pending purchases and Family Sharing</h2>
    <p>
      A purchase marked <strong>Pending</strong> has not completed through
      Apple, so {app.name} cannot unlock the paid exams yet. This can happen
      while Ask to Buy approval or another App Store payment step is waiting.
      The library unlocks after StoreKit reports a completed entitlement.
    </p>
    <p>
      Family Sharing depends on Apple’s purchase eligibility, Purchase Sharing,
      and family settings. On a family member’s device, confirm those settings,
      use the same Apple Account expected to receive the shared purchase, and
      run Restore Purchases. Apple decides whether a purchase is eligible and
      available to the family. Refund requests are also handled by Apple,
      including through
      <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com/">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Use {app.name} offline</h2>
    <p>
      Exam and course content is bundled with the app and remains readable
      offline. Study progress is recorded in the local SwiftData store, so you
      can continue studying without a connection. iCloud sync and App Store
      purchase or restore checks require Apple’s services and may wait until the
      device is online.
    </p>

    <h2>Troubleshoot iCloud sync</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Confirm each device is signed in to the intended Apple Account, iCloud
        is available, and {app.name} is allowed to use iCloud.
      </li>
      <li>
        Connect each device to the internet and open {app.name}. CloudKit
        controls sync timing, so changes may not appear immediately.
      </li>
      <li>
        Check available iCloud storage and Apple’s iCloud service status if sync
        remains paused.
      </li>
      <li>
        Do not delete the app while troubleshooting if the device may hold the
        only local copy of recent progress.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      {COMPANY.name} does not operate a progress server and cannot retrieve,
      merge, or restore study history from one.
    </p>

    <h2>Reminders, widget, and Live Activity</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Daily reminder:</strong> Turn on Daily study reminder in
      {app.name} Settings. If permission was denied, enable notifications in
      Apple Settings for {app.name}. Focus modes and Scheduled Summary can also
      delay how a local notification appears.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Widget:</strong> Open {app.name} after studying so its extension
      can refresh the latest on-device summary. If a widget remains stale,
      remove it from the Home Screen and add it again.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Live Activity:</strong> The countdown appears while a timed Exam
      Sandbox is running. Make sure Live Activities are allowed for {app.name}
      in Apple Settings. Dynamic Island presentation is available only on
      supported iPhone models; the Lock Screen presentation does not require a
      Dynamic Island.
    </p>

    <h2>Independent study material</h2>
    <p>
      {app.name} is independent and is not affiliated with or endorsed by
      Microsoft. Microsoft, Azure, and related names and marks belong to
      Microsoft. Practice content is independently authored, is not made from
      actual exam questions, and does not guarantee that you will pass an exam.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a> for app
      support. For details about data handling, read the
      <a href={app.privacyPath}>Cairn Privacy Policy</a>. Use of Cairn is subject
      to the <a href={app.termsPath}>Nintek Terms of Use</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
